################# PLEASE READ THIS FILE ## ##########################
#####################################################################

This file list changes in new versions of SUE that pose
incompatibilities to older versions.  Note that I always attempt to
keep incompatibilities to an absolute minimum.  Generally, these
incompatibilities only require changes to the .suerc file.

#####################################################################

Changes in MMI_SUE2.4

Small incompatibility with SUE version 2.3 and earlier in spice
property in an icon.  Newlines in spice properties now translate
into new lines in the netlist.  If you want to break up the text
in a spice property for better readability, you musst use a
newline FOLLOWED by a "+", i.e. the spice continuation character.
Note that the netlister will reformat this to insure that you
don't exceed the spice line length limitations.  

Note also that the inline_verilog or inline_spice routines are
being phased out.  In the future, please put all netlisting properties
in the icons only.

The use of the verilog probe has been made more general to allow other
waveform viewers than signalscan.  The old signalscan lines in .suerc
have now been combined into a single VERILOG_PROBE line.

#####################################################################
